From 13f3c59f7af60bb94b6bd21a8be4687c09ddaa9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:32:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: passthrough backend: sole mode presents on the back,
 front time measured

Timed on the GPU front in an MKW race (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_TIMES=1, new: idle, acquire waits, presents and
the present's host wait, logged every 5 s): ~380 ms/s waiting on acquires, ~80 ms/s presenting, 0 idle; the
rest is work (~43 ms of front CPU per frame at ~12.5 fps). In sole mode the guest syncpoint moves on the
front as it parses (SoleSyncpoint), so the present's syncpoint action ran Composite there: ~6.5 ms a frame
(a CPU de-tile of the frame) in which nothing was parsed or submitted. The action now queues the present
(Nx2Passthrough::DeferToBack) and the front hands it to the split's back, otherwise idle in sole mode, when
the entry is done or suspended (the action runs under the syncpoint manager's lock, which the back takes:
deferring there could deadlock on a full ring).

MKW race (racing chunks): 12.0 / 14.0 fps (12.3 / 13.3 before); presents 0 ms/s on the front; frames right.
The front is the critical path: work plus acquire waits fill the frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
